  "practice": [
    "Say ঐ three times with an oi sound like the oy in boy: oi, oi, oi.",
    "Practice ঐ-কার: ক + ৈ = কৈ, ব + ৈ = বৈ, and স + ৈ = সৈ.",
    "Remember that ৈ is written visually before its consonant even though its sound comes after it.",
    "Use the reading shortcut ৈ → oi in বৈঠক, সৈনিক, and হৈচৈ."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ঐ is a Bengali vowel with an approximate oi sound similar to the sound in English boy.",
    "When ঐ combines with a consonant, it uses the ৈ vowel sign, called ঐ-কার.",
    "The ৈ sign is written visually before its consonant, but its vowel sound follows the consonant.",
    "বই (book) also has an oi sound, but it is spelled with ই; words such as বৈঠক use the actual ৈ sign."
  ]
